speechtext:
That, in the opinion of this House, a new constitution for Canada should specifically commit Canada to the goals of
(a)	promoting international peace and security;
(b)	maintaining just and honourable relations between nations;
(c)	fostering respect for international law and treaty obligations;
(d)	encouraging the settlement of international disputes by arbitration; and
(e)	transferring agreed national powers to world authorities when this would
facilitate world peace.
